description:
Context: During a regional slowpath last week we observed rapid circuit flicker and a cascade of tenant failovers when short-term error spikes crossed thresholds. This PR introduces two coordinated mitigations: (1) a hysteresis layer on circuit transitions to prevent quick reopen/close oscillation and (2) a tenant-weighted shedding policy that biases shedding decisions away from small, latency-sensitive tenants during transient overloads. Motivation: avoid noisy failovers and keep critical tenants online during short bursts, improving SLO stability and reducing incident MTTR. Summary of changes and rationale: - pkg/circuit/hysteresis.go: New state machine wrapper that enforces a configurable open->half-open->closed hysteresis window and a cooldown backoff. This prevents flip-flopping when probes produce intermittent errors. - controllers/tenant_shedder.go: Introduces tenant weights (configurable per-tenant) and a weighted-shed algorithm that respects per-tenant importance and recent success rates. Default weights are neutral; policy is conservative. - pkg/slo/enforcer.go: Wire up hysteresis signals into SLO decision logic and add a short-term dampening multiplier so small bursts don't immediately escalate to regional failover. - telemetry/metrics.yaml: New metrics and logging for hysteresis transitions (circuit_hysteresis_state) and per-tenant-shed decisions (tenant_shed_decision{tenant,weight,reason}). - e2e/region_slowpath_test.go: Integration test that simulates a transient 30s error spike and asserts no global tenant failover and no more than one circuit transition within the cooldown window. Commits (high-level): - 7f3c8b2: add hysteresis state wrapper and tests - 1a2b9e4: tenant-weighted shedding controller and config - 9d4e1f0: integrate hysteresis with slo enforcer; add metrics - 3c6d4af: add integration test for regional slowpath and minor logging tweaks Files changed (high level): - pkg/circuit/hysteresis.go (new) - pkg/circuit/hysteresis_test.go (new) - controllers/tenant_shedder.go (modified) - pkg/slo/enforcer.go (modified) - telemetry/metrics.yaml (modified) - e2e/region_slowpath_test.go (new) - config/defaults.yaml (modified) - docs/observability/hysteresis.md (new) Small code excerpt (hysteresis guard): "// allow transition only if stable window has elapsed
if now.Sub(s.lastTransition) < s.cooldown {
    return ErrCooldown
}
// require N-success probes before closing
if s.successCount < s.closeThreshold {
    return ErrNotEnoughSuccesses
}
" Testing & CI: - Unit tests: added coverage for hysteresis and weighted-shedding logic. - Integration e2e: added region slowpath simulator. - CI: initial run had a flaky e2e (timeout in container network simulation); rerun passed and all checks green. Rollout and safety: - Feature gated behind config: defaults keep hysteresis conservative (cooldown=45s, closeThreshold=3). - Gradual rollout: enabled for 10% of regional traffic via feature flag, telemetry monitored for 24 hours before full rollout. - Emergency revert: branch provides a single toggle to set hysteresis_tracing=false and revert to previous circuit behavior. Observability: - New dashboards: Circuit hystereses (per-region), Tenant-shed heatmap. - Alerts: added alert if a circuit flips more than 3x in 10 minutes despite hysteresis enabled. Review conversation (selected): - Jordan K: "Hysteresis looks good; please ensure cooldown default is not too long for high-throughput tenants." - Maya: "Set conservative cooldown = 45s; can be lowered per-tenant via config. Added tests demonstrating no user-visible regression in low-latency tenants." - Diego A: "Concern: tenant weights could be misused to avoid shedding. Add bounds and a max-weight cap." - Maya: "Added validation on weights (0.1-10.0) and a server-side clamp at decision time. Documented in config/defaults.yaml." - Priya N: "Please add telemetry labels for region and route so we can correlate with SLO graphs." - Maya: "Done; metrics include region and route labels. Updated docs/observability/hysteresis.md." CI logs (summary): - build: pass - unit-tests: pass (coverage increased +1.4%) - integration-e2e: pass (2 runs; one rerun) - lint: pass Merge outcome: Merged by release-bot via squash on 2026-02-22 after green CI and 2 approvals. Backport/Follow-ups: - Follow-up task ENG-1499 to add a UI toggle in the Console for tenant weights and rollout percentage. - Backport hotfix to release/2026-02-xx if customer incidents reported. Notes for on-call: If you see an unexpected increase in tenant_shed_decision{reason="weight_cap"}, investigate weight updates and validate no one modified tenant config outside of the Console. End of PR description.
